# READMEs — no CI churn

Do not add bullets, sections, or paragraphs about GitHub Actions, CI workflows, path filters, pull-request checks, or “what runs in CI” to `README.md` files (or similar user-facing docs) in this repository unless the user **explicitly** requests that content.

The workflow under `.github/workflows/` is the source of truth for automation; keep it out of example READMEs by default.
